    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0392" n="318" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg318"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7924½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">House</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 26, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The conference with Clemenceau and
                        Pétain yesterday resulted in a clear
                    understanding as to the military situation. They gave us information about the
                    number of fighting men left in France and what would be necessary from us. If we
                    send over a million men by autumn 1918, they will continue to use their own
                    actual fighting men for offensive operations and use our responsibility [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">reenforcements?</hi>] for defensive purposes until
                    then.</p>
                <p>
                    Pétain believes that whatever Supreme
                    War Council is created should have a president or executive officer to execute
                    its decisions. This is sure to meet with English opposition. What is your
                    opinion of it? The English arrive to-morrow night, and on Wednesday Lloyd George, Clemenceau and I will have a conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
